            <ArticleTitle>[Measurement of regional myocardial perfusion by computer analysis of digital coronary angiograms].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1618-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Digital techniques applied to coronary angiograms provide clinically important information on the effect of stenosis on distal myocardial perfusion. During hyperemia, the delayed appearance and maximal density times in poststenotic areas are visualized on parametric images.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
